@page "/third-party"

<Seo Canonical="/third-party" Title="Blazorise Third-Party" Description="Review the third-party providers Blazorise uses, why we use them, and the personal data they may process." />

<PageHeader>
    <Title>
        Third-Party
    </Title>
    <Description>
        <Paragraph>
            We use a limited number of providers to operate Blazorise, communicate with customers, deliver marketing, and process purchases. This page explains what we share with them.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            <Strong>Version 1.0 · Effective August 31, 2026</Strong>
        </Paragraph>
    </Description>
</PageHeader>

<Row>
    <Column Margin="Margin.Is4.FromTop">
        <Container Class="terms-content">
            <Row>
                <Column ColumnSize="ColumnSize.Is8" Margin="Margin.IsAuto.OnX">
                    <Paragraph>
                        Megabit d.o.o., trading as Blazorise, is responsible for selecting providers that process personal data on our behalf and for using appropriate contractual and transfer safeguards. A provider's legal role depends on the service: it may act as our processor, as an independent controller under its own privacy policy, or in both roles for different activities. For more information about our processing and your rights, read our <Anchor To="privacy" Title="Privacy Policy">Privacy Policy</Anchor>.
                    </Paragraph>

                    <OrderedList>
                        <OrderedListItem Padding="Padding.Is3.FromBottom">
                            <Strong>Contact, Sales, and Marketing Providers</Strong>
                            <Paragraph>
                                For these services, the personal data we provide is normally limited to an email address and, where available, first and last name. Depending on your interaction, it may also include your company, role, communication preferences, the content of a form or message, and delivery or engagement information such as sends, opens, clicks, replies, bounces, and unsubscribes.
                            </Paragraph>
                            <UnorderedList>
                                <UnorderedListItem>
                                    <Paragraph>
                                        <Strong>HubSpot</Strong> — customer relationship management, contact forms, sales pipeline management, and customer communications. <Anchor To="https://legal.hubspot.com/privacy-policy" Target="Target.Blank" Title="HubSpot Privacy Policy">Privacy information</Anchor>.
                                    </Paragraph>
                                </UnorderedListItem>
                                <UnorderedListItem>
                                    <Paragraph>
                                        <Strong>Brevo</Strong> — newsletter subscriptions, email campaign delivery, contact list management, and unsubscribe handling. <Anchor To="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/" Target="Target.Blank" Title="Brevo Privacy Policy">Privacy information</Anchor>.
                                    </Paragraph>
                                </UnorderedListItem>
                                <UnorderedListItem>
                                    <Paragraph>
                                        <Strong>Instantly</Strong> — business outreach, email delivery, campaign management, and response management. <Anchor To="https://instantly.ai/privacy" Target="Target.Blank" Title="Instantly Privacy Policy">Privacy information</Anchor>.
                                    </Paragraph>
                                </UnorderedListItem>
                                <UnorderedListItem>
                                    <Paragraph>
                                        <Strong>Zoho Mail</Strong> — business email hosting and communication. Zoho may process sender and recipient names and email addresses, message content and attachments, and technical delivery metadata. <Anchor To="https://www.zoho.com/privacy.html" Target="Target.Blank" Title="Zoho Privacy Policy">Privacy information</Anchor>.
                                    </Paragraph>
                                </UnorderedListItem>
                            </UnorderedList>
                        </OrderedListItem>
                        <OrderedListItem Padding="Padding.Is3.FromBottom">
                            <Strong>Purchases and Billing</Strong>
                            <UnorderedList>
                                <UnorderedListItem>
                                    <Paragraph>
                                        <Strong>Paddle</Strong> — merchant of record and authorized reseller for online purchases. Paddle processes identity, contact, billing, payment, transaction, tax, fraud-prevention, and device information needed to complete and support a purchase. Paddle acts as an independent controller for much of this processing under its own terms and privacy policy. Blazorise receives order and entitlement information but does not store full payment card details. <Anchor To="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy" Target="Target.Blank" Title="Paddle Privacy Policy">Privacy information</Anchor>.
                                    </Paragraph>
                                </UnorderedListItem>
                            </UnorderedList>
                        </OrderedListItem>
                        <OrderedListItem Padding="Padding.Is3.FromBottom">
                            <Strong>Website Operation and Measurement</Strong>
                            <UnorderedList>
                                <UnorderedListItem>
                                    <Paragraph>
                                        <Strong>Plausible Analytics</Strong> — aggregated website audience measurement. Plausible is configured without tracking cookies and provides aggregated usage statistics. Requests may still include technical information such as an IP address and user agent, which Plausible handles according to its documentation. <Anchor To="https://plausible.io/data-policy" Target="Target.Blank" Title="Plausible Data Policy">Privacy information</Anchor>.
                                    </Paragraph>
                                </UnorderedListItem>
                                <UnorderedListItem>
                                    <Paragraph>
                                        <Strong>Google reCAPTCHA</Strong> — form security, spam prevention, and abuse detection. Google may receive technical and interaction data, including IP address, browser and device information, cookies, and interaction signals, under Google's terms and privacy policy. <Anchor To="https://policies.google.com/privacy" Target="Target.Blank" Title="Google Privacy Policy">Privacy information</Anchor>.
                                    </Paragraph>
                                </UnorderedListItem>
                                <UnorderedListItem>
                                    <Paragraph>
                                        <Strong>jsDelivr and cdnjs</Strong> — delivery of website styles and scripts. When your browser requests an asset, the delivery provider may receive the requested URL, IP address, user agent, referrer, and request time as part of ordinary web-server logs. See the <Anchor To="https://www.jsdelivr.com/terms/sub-processors" Target="Target.Blank" Title="jsDelivr Sub-Processors">jsDelivr provider information</Anchor> and <Anchor To="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" Target="Target.Blank" Title="Cloudflare Privacy Policy">Cloudflare privacy policy</Anchor> for cdnjs.
                                    </Paragraph>
                                </UnorderedListItem>
                            </UnorderedList>
                        </OrderedListItem>
                        <OrderedListItem Padding="Padding.Is3.FromBottom">
                            <Strong>International Processing</Strong>
                            <Paragraph>
                                A provider may process data in more than one country, including outside the European Economic Area. Where required, we rely on recognized safeguards such as adequacy decisions or the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses. Provider locations, affiliates, and subprocessors may change; the linked provider information is the best source for current details.
                            </Paragraph>
                        </OrderedListItem>
                        <OrderedListItem Padding="Padding.Is3.FromBottom">
                            <Strong>Changes and Questions</Strong>
                            <Paragraph>
                                We update this list when our key providers or their roles change. A provider may be replaced by another provider performing a similar function. If a change materially affects how we process personal data, we will provide additional notice where required. Questions about this list may be sent to <Strong>support@blazorise.com</Strong>.
                            </Paragraph>
                        </OrderedListItem>
                    </OrderedList>
                </Column>
            </Row>
        </Container>
    </Column>
</Row>